# Local settings of one checkout (git ignores `.env`). Docker Compose reads this file, and so does the pre-push hook.
# Only needed when two checkouts or worktrees run at the same time: give each its own project name and host ports, so that their
# containers and databases never meet (docs/testing/README.md, "Two checkouts at once"). The defaults suit a single checkout.

# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=botrts-feature-a
# POSTGRES_PORT=15432
# REDIS_PORT=16379

# The tests read the database from DATABASE_URL (the pre-push hook builds it from POSTGRES_PORT) and two Redis tests from REDIS_URL.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://botrts:botrts@localhost:15432/botrts
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:16379
